  "prompt": "=== Chain-of-thought analysis prompt ===\nYou are a software requirements analyst preparing a UML state machine model.\n\nAnalyze the requirement and extract only the modeling facts needed for a state transition diagram. Keep the analysis concise and evidence-based.\n\nReturn the analysis using exactly these headings:\nStates:\nInitial state:\nFinal states:\nEvents or conditions:\nTransitions:\nMissing or ambiguous details:\n\nDo not write PlantUML in this step.\n\nRequirement:\nGreen Rides — Polished Requirement Specification\n\nFunctional Requirements\n1. The system shall display journey details upon user login and destination selection.\n2. The system shall allow users to activate driving mode or choose other options after viewing journey details.\n3. The system shall enable users to select a place to eat, view its menu, and place an order if they are hungry.\n4. The system shall inform relevant authorities in the event of an accident.\n5. The system shall send notifications during driving or in case of an accident.\n6. The system shall allow users to provide feedback upon completion of their journey.\n\n=== Chain-of-thought analysis response ===\nStates:\nLogged In, Journey Details Displayed, Driving Mode, Eating Mode, Accident Reported, Feedback Provided\n\nInitial state:\nLogged In\n\nFinal states:\nFeedback Provided\n\nEvents or conditions:\nLogin, Destination Selection, Activate Driving Mode, Select Eating Place, View Menu, Place Order, Accident, Journey Completion, Provide Feedback\n\nTransitions:\nLogged In -> Journey Details Displayed (Login, Destination Selection)\nJourney Details Displayed -> Driving Mode (Activate Driving Mode)\nJourney Details Displayed -> Eating Mode (Select Eating Place)\nEating Mode -> Eating Mode (View Menu, Place Order)\nDriving Mode -> Accident Reported (Accident)\nDriving Mode -> Feedback Provided (Journey Completion)\nAccident Reported -> Driving Mode (Resume Driving - *implied*)\nEating Mode -> Feedback Provided 